{"title":"Career Roadmap: Textile Quality Manager","role":"Textile Quality Manager","summary":"A Textile Quality Manager is responsible for maintaining and improving the quality of textile materials and finished products across processes such as spinning, weaving, knitting, dyeing, printing, finishing, garmenting, and technical textiles.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Textile & Fashion Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Textile Quality Manager is responsible for maintaining and improving the quality of textile materials and finished products across processes such as spinning, weaving, knitting, dyeing, printing, finishing, garmenting, and technical textiles."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Textile Technology","Quality Engineering","Testing","Process Control","Supply-Chain Quality","Data Analytics","Leadership"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Establishing quality standards"},{"text":"Monitoring production quality"},{"text":"Laboratory testing"},{"text":"Defect analysis"},{"text":"Supplier quality management"},{"text":"Customer complaint resolution"},{"text":"CAPA and root-cause analysis"},{"text":"Statistical process control"},{"text":"Quality audits"},{"text":"Quality-system implementation"},{"text":"Continuous improvement"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"QC Engineer / Textile Quality Engineer / Quality Trainee"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Senior Quality Engineer / Quality Assurance Engineer / Supplier Quality Engineer"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Quality Manager / QA Manager / Textile Quality Specialist"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Head of Quality / Quality Director / Technical & Quality Consultant"}]]}]},{"